<title>INDIA: India Ciba 96/97 1st half net up 10 pct.</title>
<headline>India Ciba 96/97 1st half net up 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30,1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   176.2 vs    160.2</p>
<p>    Net sales	  3,043.7 vs  2,518.9</p>
<p>    Other income	 141.5 vs     81.1</p>
<p>    Expenditure	2,739.0 vs  2,253.4</p>
<p>    Interest		86.7 vs     26.9</p>
<p>    Gross profit	 359.5 vs    319.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  83.5 vs     72.9</p>
<p>    Taxation		99.8 vs     86.6</p>
<p>Note: Hindustan Ciba-Geigy Ltd is the Indian subsidiary of Swiss multinational Ciba. The firm said its board approved of schemes for demerger of its speciality chemicals business and merger of Sandoz India with the firm. It will seek shareholders approval for these on December 10.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
